        "message": "A first look at the species range data for the California plant heat-vulnerability tool. 99 species are here as separate layers (Calflora climate-model distributions, scored 0-9) - toggle them in the layer menu.\n\nTwo things to note. Cells scoring 0 are drawn pale and cells scoring 1 or above are red; across all 99 species only about 2% of scored cells exceed zero, so ranges look sparse at statewide zoom - zoom in to see them. Whether a species' range should be read as every scored cell, every cell above zero, or every cell above some higher cutoff is exactly the question we have back to the data providers.\n\nThe LOCA2 temperature projections are not loaded yet, so the exceedance-day calculation this tool is ultimately for is not available in this preview.",
